      "text": "Fig. 5. (a) Relative base case breakthrough times for all PFAA normalized to PFOA. (b) Relative breakthrough times of individual PFAA under changes in water chemistry normalized to the base case condition. Base case, 1 mM NaHCO 3 , pH = 7.5; \u25ab I = 100 mM, NaCl; SRNOM2 = 10 mg/L. R.A. Mol \u00b4e et al. Journal of Hazardous Materials 474 (2024) 134746 8 future work should include engineering new injectable CAC materials with properties that can enhance the performance for short chain PFAA. This could include highly defunctionalized carbon materials with elevated anion exchange capacities to offset competition from inorganic anions. To mitigate the impact of organic matter, one approach could be engineering an adsorptive material with precise pore size distributions that obstruct DOM from entering micropores and only allow for short- chain PFAA adsorption. There is also the potential to design barriers to account for differences between long- and short-chain PFAA. This could include the addition of multiple injectable phases such as ion exchange resins [20] and adsorptive materials which take advantage of the properties of both short- and long-chain PFAA present at a site [21] . Environmental implication Subsurface injection of colloidal activated carbon (CAC) is an emerging in situ approach to treat perfluoroalkyl acid (PFAA)-impacted"
